#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0693 expect=skipped domain=ADLBC
#note "Firing data under a degraded key, but PARAMCD alone detects plain BASIC DATA STRUCTURE and the rule's Include is [MEDICAL DEVICE BASIC DATA STRUCTURE] ALONE - the supertype relation runs MD-BDS -> BDS and NEVER the other way, so a plain BDS dataset is out of scope. This is the fixture that proves the MD token is load-bearing here, unlike the redundant pairs recorded on AD0149B-F1. No SPDEVID column."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col BASE    type=Num
col BASEC   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC | 1 | LOW
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC | 2 | LOW
